; Two readings of `das Mädchen`, put to one row set.
; Reading A — the neuter marks the referent's social standing (a young woman held as a
; thing until marriage). Reading B — the neuter marks the composition's diminutive.
; Rows chosen to separate them: a grown man's diminutive, a house, a young male with no
; diminutive. Five digits, low to high: A mispredicts two of four; B mispredicts none;
; B is the closer fit; Männchen acks neuter (so: not about being female); Junge acks
; masculine (so: not about being young).
;
; The social history the reading points at is real and is not what this band tests.
; What it tests is whether the NEUTER carries it. It does not.
import "../word-gender-derivation.fk"
; witnessed: 2026-07-28 -> 11111, four-way (go/rust/ts all 11111)
(word-gender-standing-check)
